sg-compositor (0.2.0+sg5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Display power: wlr-output-power-management-unstable-v1, so wlopm and
    Settings' "Turn off the screen after" (swayidle) turn the screen off; the
    output is disabled in place (no window moves, XWayland keeps its size)
    and any input turns it back on. The output a Remote Desktop session is
    captured from is never turned off. Gate: make test-power (swayidle
    timeouts, input resetting them, idle inhibitors).

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:20:00 -0700

sg-compositor (0.2.0+sg4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remote Desktop takes over the console session (E1b): REMOTE on the control
    socket (lock account or root; optionally with the RDP daemon's end of a
    socketpair as the remote connection) moves the user's windows to a new
    headless output at the console's size, unlocks, and ignores the console's
    own keyboard, pointer and touch; Ctrl+Alt+Del at the console, LOCAL, or
    the remote connection closing gives the session back locked, and the
    remote connection loses it at once. view_center honours the output's
    offset.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:02:27 -0700

sg-compositor (0.2.0+sg3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An output with no modes of its own (headless: a Remote Desktop session)
    takes its size from SG_OUTPUT_SIZE=WxH, the RDP client's desktop size,
    instead of wlroots' fixed 1280x720.

